      "mathematicalReason": "The square has side length 1 inch. Right triangles DCM and BCN have equal hypotenuses CM=CN and equal legs DC=BC, so HL gives DM=BN. Hence AM=AN=t, where 0<t<1. Equilateral side equality and Pythagoras give MN²=2t²=CM²=1+(1−t)². Thus (t+1)²=3, and the admissible root is t=√3−1. Subtracting the three corner triangles from the square gives [CMN]=1−t²/2−(1−t)=2√3−3. This supports the equilateral-triangle and triangle-area assessments and the listed congruence and composite-area support. The alternative route is also valid: the equal angles DCM and BCN total 30°, so each is 15°, and DM=tan(45°−30°)=2−√3.",
