      "mathematicalReason": "Because M is the midpoint of BC and G lies on AM, triangles ABG and ACG have equal areas. Therefore [AFG]/[AEG]=(AF/AB)/(AE/AC)=(AF/12)/(2AF/16)=2/3. Triangles AFG and AEG share the same altitude to line EF, so GF/GE=2/3 and EG/GF=3/2. This directly supports proportional-segment manipulation, with median and triangle-area facts supplying one valid route. The similarity route is also defensible: draw the parallel to BC through E, meeting AB at H and AM at K. Similarity gives AH=3AF/2 and HK=KE. A second parallel through F, meeting AM at J, gives FJ/EK=2/3; similarity of triangles FJG and EKG then yields GF/GE=2/3.",
