      "derivedAnswer": "B: figure II.",
      "mathematicalReason": "For a>0, the sublevel set 2Max(|x|,|y|)≤a is the axis-aligned square with vertices (±a/2,±a/2). The sublevel set √(2(x²+y²))≤a is the disk x²+y²≤a²/2, whose radius is a/√2. Finally, |x|+|y|≤a is the diamond with vertices (±a,0) and (0,±a). The specified reversal of inequality into sublevel-set containment therefore requires an axis-aligned square inside a circle inside a diamond, exactly figure II. At a=0 all three sets are the origin, and for a<0 all are empty. The candidate scopes appropriately cover containment, coordinate descriptions of the squares, and recognition of the circle equation; proving the displayed inequalities by a separate inequality theorem is not necessary.",
